antage":-0.00997040983938579,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":30.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.0764186026932824,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03200981406780712,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":10.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0689430894308943,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.048460003,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":32.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Eton Pharmaceuticals, Inc., a pharmaceutical company, focuses on developing and commercializing treatments for rare diseases. Its commercial rare disease products include Increlex for the treatment of severe primary igf-1 deficiency; Alkindi Sprinkle for adrenal insufficiency; Khindivi for adrenocortical insufficiency; Galzin for Wilson disease; PKU Golike for phenylketonuria; Carglumic Acid for N-acetylglutamate synthase deficiency; Betaine Anhydrous for homocystinuria; and Nitisinone for tyrosinemia type 1. The company is also developing various product candidates, which are in late-stage development, including ET-600 for diabetes insipidus; Amglidia for neonatal diabetes mellitus; ET-700 for Wilson disease; ET-800 for adrenal insufficiency; and ZENEO hydrocortisone autoinjector for adrenal crisis. Eton Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was incorporated in 2017 and is based in Deer Park, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sean E. Brynjelsen | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 44 people. Revenue per employee of $1.8M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 109%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $232K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $125K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Eton Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.9B market cap on $80M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +56% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +323.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -25% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 60% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $10M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin -0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 874% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":8.736224206811757},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $23.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(ETON) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/ETON_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_112626043401_1795685641.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795685641.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Earnings Estimates Moving Higher for Eton Pharmaceuticals (ETON): Time to Buy?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3032721/earnings-estimates-moving-higher-for-eton-pharmaceuticals-eton-time-to-buy?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_8-3032721","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795105201.0,"origin":"tiingo","sen